bug_report:
(a * b) != 0 then we know that both a!=0 & b != 0
Take:
```
int fa(int a, int b)
{
  int c = a * b;
  if (c != 0)
    return (a != 0);
  return 0;
}
int fb(int a, int b)
{
  int c = a * b;
  if (c != 0)
    return (b != 0);
  return 0;
}
```

This should optimize to just `return (a*b) != 0` (well rather `a & b != 0` but that is for a different issue). as we know if we multiply together 2 integers then both of them has to be non-zero.

This is the missing optimization that is causingPR 110992not to be optimized any more after the `&-` -> `*` simplification.
